course: dictionary
lesson: 4217
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can tell which one is meant by reading the words around it. The context is the clue. «Losing with good grace and learning from it helps you get better.» Here grace is not about a girl's name or a prayer. It means losing in a calm, polite way.
explain: Grace can also describe how someone moves. Dancers and gymnasts move with grace, which means smoothly, beautifully and easily. When you meet grace, ask: which meaning fits here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some phrases use grace in set ways. Say grace means to say a short prayer of thanks before a meal. A grace period is extra time before something must be done. Saving grace means one good thing that makes up for something bad. A phrase like this is best learned as a whole.
fact: Grace is a noun and also a verb in formal writing.
fact: Grace means a smooth, beautiful and easy way of moving.
fact: Grace also means being polite, kind and calm, even when things are hard.
fact: Say grace means a short prayer of thanks said before a meal, and a grace period is extra time before something must be done.
fact: Grace is also a girl's name, so with a capital letter it may be a person, as in «Grace and Bella went to the park».
exercise: «Losing with good grace and learning from it helps you get better.» What does good grace mean here? | Refusing to play again | * Losing calmly and politely | Winning by cheating | Crying loudly and running away
exercise: The dancer leapt across the stage with grace. What does grace mean? | Being very loud | * Smooth, beautiful and easy movement | A short prayer before dinner | A rude shout
exercise: Which word means a short prayer of thanks said before a meal? | silence | table | sweet | * grace
test: The school gave us a grace period, so we had an extra week to hand in our project. What does grace period mean? | A prize for the best project | * Extra time allowed before something must be done | A long lesson in the hall | A week of holidays from school
test: Which word best fits? Zara crossed the ice with ___ and never wobbled. | anger | rush | noise | * grace
exam: In which sentence is grace a girl's name? | «Please say grace before you start eating.» | «She showed grace when she lost the match.» | «He moved with grace across the room.» | * «Grace is coming to my party on Saturday.»
